# Writing notes, with every prompt of nanny's CON_NOTE_* states. In the temple (3001): Decimus (10), Quintus (25) and
# Smokegod (60, an immortal, so it chooses when a note expires). The boards start empty. General must include "all"
# (it's added), Ideas defaults to "all" on an empty line, Personal must not include "all", and only immortals post on
# Announce. Then the notes in progress. A tell to someone writing one. A second login as a character who's writing a
# note closes the writer's connection, as a "double newbie", and says "Illegal name" (#66); the character is left
# link-dead with its note, so logging in again reconnects it. So Quintus continues its note; Decimus, with no text
# yet, has its note cancelled; and Smokegod quits with a note in progress. Before that, Decimus, Quintus and Smokegod
# post notes one pulse apart, so two fall in the same second, and the second one's stamp is the first's plus one.
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@connect quin
Quintus
psswrd
@return
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
@as dec
note write
Quintus
@return
This subject line is far too long to be accepted by the board, at 61.
Hello there
line one
this line is more than eighty characters long, so the note board rejects it outright
   indented, and with a ~tilde~
~
x
@return
v
c
END
p
